claim.claim-text:
tubular insulation (100) having a longitudinal slit (400);
a jacket (110) overlaying the outer surface of the tubular insulation, wherein the jacket has an extended lip portion (200) extending beyond the longitudinal slit;
an internal release liner (130) attached to the extended lip portion (200) and positioned so that a portion of the internal release liner (130) reaches beyond the extended lip portion (200), wherein an edge of the internal release liner (130) is adjacent to an edge of the extended lip portion (200) forming a second lip (3200);
a first adhesive (420) located on a first side of the internal release liner (130) that is attached to the extended lip portion (200); and
a second adhesive (210) located on a second side of the internal release liner (130) on the second lip (3200).

tubular insulation (100) having a longitudinal slit (400);
a jacket (110) overlaying the outer surface of the tubular insulation (100), wherein the jacket (110) has an extended lip portion (200) extending beyond the longitudinal slit (400);
a first adhesive (420) located on the extended lip portion (200), wherein the first adhesive (420) is located between the extended lip portion (200) and the jacket (110);
a second adhesive (210) located on the extended lip portion (200), wherein the second adhesive (210) is located between the extended lip portion (200) and the jacket (110); and
an internal release liner (130) located between the first adhesive (420) and the jacket (110), wherein the internal release liner (130) covers the first adhesive (420),
wherein each of the first adhesive (420) and the second adhesive (210) contacts the extended lip portion (200), and
wherein a gap separates the first adhesive (420) and the second adhesive (210).
